-- §22 What each fusion declared it cannot see: the offsets between its own parts.
# One row per unordered pair of parts inside one fusion: the rate at which one part's supply
# substitutes for the other's, and the sentence the composer wrote to license it.
#
# What the rate means
#   A fusion adds its parts after converting each by its own factor, so moving `d` of part A's own
#   supply out and `d * phi_A / phi_B` of part B's in leaves the composed figure exactly where it
#   was. `phi_A / phi_B` is that exchange rate, in the parts' own units, and the pair is a
#   generator of the fusion's block of the composition map's null space.
#   Proof: `src/proofs/README.md`, entry `composition_kernel`.
#
# A report, and it must never become a rule
#   `asrt:Fusion` says the fungibility judgement is the composer's and that no validator reaches
#   it: whether a unit of supply in one part can serve demand in the other is a claim about the
#   world, not about the arithmetic. So this relation carries no verdict and accuses nobody. What
#   it does is put a magnitude beside the claim, because `asrt:Fusion/observed` asks for the
#   judgement to be written where a reader can disagree with it, and a reader disagreeing needs
#   to know how much is being asserted rather than only that something is.
#
# The conformance row it answers, which had no relation at all
#   `conformance/README.md` carries "a fusion's parts are fungible, so their remainders may
#   offset" with no rule beside it, and `asrt:Fusion` names the damage of getting it wrong: a
#   group remainder smaller than reality, because one member's excess covered another's shortfall
#   across a boundary nothing can cross. That sentence is about this rate. Nothing measured it.
#
# A one-part fusion has no row, and that is the whole of its claim
#   With one part there is no sibling to substitute for, so the block is zero and the fusion
#   asserts no fungibility whatever. Its absence here is the finding, not a gap.
#
# ⛔ The row count is NOT the dimension, and today it happens to equal it
#   This relation returns one row per PAIR, so a fusion of `k` parts gives `C(k, 2)` rows while
#   its block of the null space has dimension `k - 1`. Those agree at `k` of 1 and 2 and part
#   company at 3, where three pairs span two dimensions and the third pair is the sum of the other
#   two. Every fusion in this corpus is binary, so the totals agree here for a reason that is a
#   fact about the corpus rather than about the arithmetic. `rank/composition_kernel.sqlc` is the
#   dimension and this relation is not; summing these rows to get one would be right today and
#   wrong at the first fusion with three parts.
#   `eliminations/derived.sqlc` pairs the other projection of this incidence and carries the same
#   caveat, which is why neither relation's row count may be read as a correction.
#
# An absent factor leaves the rate undetermined, and says so
#   `asrt:Part/factor` may be filed as a typed absence, and then the rate is not a number anybody
#   can write. The pair still exists and the fusion still added them, so the row stays and
#   `determined` is false with `undetermined_because` naming the part whose factor is missing. A
#   blank rate and a rate of one are different facts, and collapsing them would report a fusion
#   as asserting an exchange at par when nobody said so.
#
# Corner discipline on a quotient of two factors
#   The two factors are different parts' and are filed independently, so the quotient takes its
#   low at `phi_A_low / phi_B_high` and its high at `phi_A_high / phi_B_low` with no symbol
#   repeated. A part with no factor at all converts at exactly one, which is a point and not a
#   range, so it contributes no width of its own.
#
# Unordered, and the reflexive pair is dropped
#   A part does not substitute for itself, and naming the pair twice would say the fusion declared
#   two offsets where it declared one. The row comparison keeps each pair once, the same idiom
#   `eliminations/derived.sqlc` uses for the other projection of this incidence.
-- asrt:Fusion/asrt:Part crossed with itself on the fusion, carrying each part's factor.
WITH
notations AS NOT MATERIALIZED (
    :define(composition/notations.sqlc)
),
part_references AS NOT MATERIALIZED (
    :define(composition/part_references.sqlc)
),
parts AS NOT MATERIALIZED (
    :define(composition/parts.sqlc)
),
fusions AS NOT MATERIALIZED (
    :define(composition/fusions.sqlc)
),
sized AS (
    SELECT p.composition, p.composed_layer,
           p.part_filing, p.part_layer, p.factor_state,
           CASE WHEN p.factor_state = 'omitted' THEN 1 ELSE p.factor_low  END AS lo,
           CASE WHEN p.factor_state = 'omitted' THEN 1 ELSE p.factor_mode END AS md,
           CASE WHEN p.factor_state = 'omitted' THEN 1 ELSE p.factor_high END AS hi
    FROM ( :compose(composition/parts.sqlc) ) p
)
SELECT a.composition                                        AS "composition!",
       a.composed_layer                                     AS "composed_layer!",
       a.part_filing  || '/' || a.part_layer                AS "part_a!",
       b.part_filing  || '/' || b.part_layer                AS "part_b!",
       (a.lo IS NOT NULL AND b.lo IS NOT NULL)              AS "determined!",
       least(a.lo / b.hi, a.hi / b.lo)::double precision    AS rate_low,
       (a.md / b.md)::double precision                      AS rate_mode,
       greatest(a.lo / b.hi, a.hi / b.lo)::double precision AS rate_high,
       CASE WHEN a.lo IS NOT NULL AND b.lo IS NOT NULL THEN NULL
            ELSE concat_ws(' and ',
                     CASE WHEN a.lo IS NULL
                          THEN 'the factor on ' || a.part_layer || ' is ' || a.factor_state END,
                     CASE WHEN b.lo IS NULL
                          THEN 'the factor on ' || b.part_layer || ' is ' || b.factor_state END)
       END                                                  AS undetermined_because,
       f.observed                                           AS "observed!"
FROM      sized a
JOIN      sized b
       ON b.composition    = a.composition
      AND b.composed_layer = a.composed_layer
      AND (b.part_filing, b.part_layer) > (a.part_filing, a.part_layer)
JOIN      (
    :compose(composition/fusions.sqlc)
) f ON f.filing = a.composition AND f.layer = a.composed_layer
ORDER BY a.composition, a.composed_layer, "part_a!", "part_b!"
